# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Youna — Environment Variables Template
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# FLOWS AF (NEVER DO THIS):
#   ❌  Copy this file to .env.local and commit .env.local to git
#   ❌  Use these placeholder values as real credentials in production
#   ❌  Treat this file as a "ready to use" configuration
#
# CORRECT FLOWS (WHAT TO DO):
#   ✅  Copy this file to .env.local:  cp .env.local.example .env.local
#   ✅  Fill in YOUR real values for each variable you need
#   ✅  Add .env.local to .gitignore (it already is — verify with `git status`)
#   ✅  Generate secrets properly:  openssl rand -base64 32
#   ✅  Get API keys from the relevant provider dashboards
#
# This file is a TEMPLATE showing which variables Youna expects.
# Every value below is a PLACEHOLDER and will NOT work as-is.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Database (PostgreSQL — Neon, Supabase, Vercel Postgres, or local) ─────
# REQUIRED for: auth, memory, journaling, mood tracking, goals, habits,
#               subscription billing, conversation history (Phase 3+).
#
# Placeholder value below — replace with YOUR connection string.
# Format: postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DATABASE?sslmode=require
#   Neon: https://neon.tech → create project → copy connection string
#   Supabase: Settings → Database → Connection string
#   Local:  postgresql://postgres:password@localhost:5432/youna?sslmode=disable
#   Production (recommended): use sslmode=require
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_DB_USER:REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_PASSWORD@REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_HOST:5432/youna?sslmode=require"

# ── NextAuth — Authentication ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED for: user accounts, sign-in, sessions (Phase 3+).
#
# NEXTAUTH_URL — the canonical URL of your app. Must match the domain
#   where cookies are set.
#   Local dev: http://localhost:3000
#   Production: https://yourdomain.com
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# NEXTAUTH_SECRET — a random 32+ character string used to sign JWTs.
#   Generate a REAL one with:  openssl rand -base64 32
#   The value below is a placeholder and WILL NOT WORK.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXTAUTH_SECRET="REPLACE_WITH_OUTPUT_OF_openssl_rand_-base64_32"

# ── LLM Providers (optional — Youna works in mock mode without these) ───────
# Added in Phase 3 when you want real LLM responses.
# At least one of these must be set for the chat to use a real AI model.
# Without any key, Youna falls back to mock mode (Phase 1/2 behavior).
#
# Get these from the provider's developer dashboard.
# NEVER commit a real API key. If a key leaks, rotate it immediately.
#
# OpenAI (GPT-4o / GPT-4o-mini):
#   OPENAI_API_KEY="sk-proj-..."   ← real keys start with sk-proj-
#
# Anthropic (Claude Haiku / Sonnet / Opus):
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-api03-..."   ← real keys start with sk-ant-api03-
#
# Google (Gemini Flash / Pro):
#   GEMINI_API_KEY="AIza..."   ← real keys start with AIza-
#
# Local / self-hosted (LM Studio, Ollama, vLLM):
#   LM_STUDIO_API_BASE="http://localhost:1234/v1"
#   LM_STUDIO_API_KEY="lm-studio"
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPENAI_API_KEY="REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_OPENAI_API_KEY"
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"
# GEMINI_API_KEY="REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_GEMINI_API_KEY"

# ── Stripe — Billing (optional — for subscription tiers in Phase 3-4) ───────
# Required for: Premium / Pro / Ultra subscription billing, webhook processing.
# Get these from your Stripe dashboard: https://dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys
# Use test keys first (sk_test_ / pk_test_), then live keys (sk_live_ / pk_live_).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY="REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_STRIPE_SECRET_KEY"
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET="REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET"
# STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY"

# ── Plausible Analytics (optional — privacy-friendly, self-hostable) ───────
# PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN="yourdomain.com"
# PLAUSIBLE_API_KEY="..."
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Sentry (optional — error tracking) ─────────────────────────────────────
# SENTRY_DSN="https://xxx@xxx.ingest.sentry.io/xxx"
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# QUICK START (local development, no database yet):
#
#   1. Delete this file (or leave it empty) — Youna will use localStorage
#      and mock AI, which is the Phase 1/2 experience.
#
#   2. Or keep this file but ONLY fill in NEXTAUTH_URL if you want to test
#      the auth route (it will return 503 until DATABASE_URL is set).
#
# QUICK START (local development, with database):
#
#   1. Start Postgres:  docker run -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=password \
#      -p 5432:5432 postgres
#   2. Set DATABASE_URL to: postgresql://postgres:password@localhost:5432/youna
#   3. Set NEXTAUTH_SECRET to:  openssl rand -base64 32
#   4. Run:  npx prisma generate && npx prisma db push
#   5. Run:  npm run dev
#
# QUICK START (production):
#
#   1. Provision a PostgreSQL database (Neon, Supabase, Vercel Postgres, etc.)
#   2. Set all required vars in your hosting platform's environment settings
#   3. Generate a real NEXTAUTH_SECRET:  openssl rand -base64 32
#   4. Set NEXTAUTH_URL to your production domain
#   5. Add at least one LLM API key for real AI responses
#   6. Deploy
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
